    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0567" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg479"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-15T14:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. As a consequence of attack by Peruvian planes on Colombian vessels in
                    Brazilian and Colombian waters Colombian Minister at Lima has been instructed to
                    ask for passports and Peruvian Minister here was handed his this morning at
                        11.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d508-f1"/> Olaya does not intend to declare
                    war.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d508-f1" n="25" xml:id="d508-f1-content">
                <p>See section entitled “Assumption by the American Embassy in Peru of Colombian
                    Interests in Peru; Sacking of the Colombian Legation”, <ref target="#pg549">pp.
                        549</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
